        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0745" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg675"/>

                <head>No. 416.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 3, 1883</date>.
                        (Received September 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 683.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a copy of Consul
                    Viosca’s dispatch to me, No. 13, 17th August last, which informs me that the
                    circuit court at Culiacan has fully confirmed the sentence imposed by the
                    district court at La Paz upon Captain Caleb, of the American schooner Adriana,
                    and that that schooner was to have been sold in a few days (after the date of
                    his dispatch).</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d417-a1.xml" xpointer="d417-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
